From 9a2e4b223feb194b65e0d4296b38557e17316b6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Lane A <lane-a@local.invalid>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:11:36 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 05/18] feat(selection): see visual story moments; keep a clip
 running to its payoff

Root cause #1c of clip1.mp4 (handoff/quality-clip1/ROOT_CAUSE.md): selection
read only the transcript. In the clip1 source both award wins (190-244 s and
the Streamer of the Year win at ~300-378 s) have no transcribed speech (music,
applause, a speech with burned-in subtitles), so no selector could see them.

auto_director/story_events.py, SELECTION_EVENTS (default OFF until Luffy
approves, Sanji Q15): one frame every 2 s scored with the SigLIP model the
B-roll vision veto already uses, against story descriptions (award on stage,
applause, screen with content, speech on stage, celebrating, laughing,
gameplay) vs background ones; winning runs become event spans that
- join the selector's clip_signals hints (same "- [mm:ss - mm:ss]" format),
- extend a selected clip that ends inside a moment until it finishes,
- drive the no-model fallback window (strongest run x 1.5 when the transcript
  cannot see it, with a 25 s lead snapped back to the setup sentence).

media/timeline.py, CLIP_CAP_KEEP_VISUAL_TAIL (default off): the 60 s cap
walked back to the last transcribed word even when that word was 52 s
earlier, collapsing the Step 4 clip to 7.7 s; with the switch on, the cap
is kept when the last word is beyond the existing back-off limit.

Evidence: handoff/quality-clip1/step4/ - with no AI key the engine picked
297.3-357.3 s by itself: "The nominees for Streamer of the Year...", the wait,
him jumping up, the walk to the stage, the speech (story_timeline.md).
Tests: test_story_events 9/9; clip boundary/timeline suites 73/73 (switch off).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
