 ## 2026-11-18
+- **Improved:** Clip picking can now see moments that happen in the picture, not only in the words: an award walk-up, a speech with burned-in subtitles, a celebration. These moments are offered to the AI picker, and a clip that ends just as one starts now keeps going until it finishes (within the 60-second limit). Off until approved: set `SELECTION_EVENTS=on` and `CLIP_CAP_KEEP_VISUAL_TAIL=on` to try it. ([#TBD](https://github.com/FujiwaraChoki/supoclip/pulls))
 - **Fixed:** Captions no longer repeat a phrase over and over when the speech recogniser loops over loud crowd or music noise; the phrase is shown once. Caption lines now follow the phrasing of the speech (sentence ends, pauses, commas) and never leave a single word stranded on its own line. Off until approved: set `CAPTION_LOOP_FILTER=on` and `CAPTION_PHRASE_SPLIT=on` to try it. ([#TBD](https://github.com/FujiwaraChoki/supoclip/pulls))
 - **Improved:** Wide shots no longer fill the top and bottom of the frame with a blurred copy of the picture: the bars become a calm, dark tint of the shot's own colour, so captions and titles sit on a clean background. On 4K footage people are now found at a sharper resolution, so medium shots of the speaker are framed on them instead of shown tiny. Off until approved: set `FIT_PAD=ambient` and `REFRAME_HIRES_PROBE=on` to try it. ([#TBD](https://github.com/FujiwaraChoki/supoclip/pulls))
 - **Improved:** Auto edits can now cut only where the footage gives a reason: a real camera change or the end of a sentence. Before, clips were sliced into equal pieces, with zooms every few seconds and cuts snapped to the background music. Zooms now need speech behind them, and decorative transitions only land on real camera changes. Off until approved: set `EDL_CONTENT_CUTS=on` to try it. ([#TBD](https://github.com/FujiwaraChoki/supoclip/pulls))
